KONOHA NINJA ACADEMY — DISCIPLINARY RECORD
Student: Uzumaki, Naruto
Instructor of record: Iruka Umino, Chunin
Status: closed record, retained per standard seven-year policy

Incident log:

1. Hokage Monument, unauthorized modification (graffiti). All four faces defaced with
   paint. Repeat offense — this was not the first attempt, only the first successful
   one. Village cleanup crew required a full day. Third Hokage personally declined to
   press for further punishment beyond standard detention, on record as finding it
   "creative."

2. Sexy Jutsu, unauthorized classroom demonstration, disrupted written examination in
   progress. Multiple repeat incidents. Instructor Umino's notes describe this as
   "technically impressive chakra control wasted on nonsense," which the student
   apparently took as a compliment.

3. Failure to attend mandatory tutoring, x4 documented instances. Pattern noted:
   absences cluster around Ichiraku Ramen's lunch rush. Correlation flagged, not
   formally investigated.

4. Academy exam records show three prior graduation attempts before the fourth
   (successful, see academy_exam_results.xlsx) — clone jutsu deficiency each time
   until the special-case pass following the forehead-protector incident. See
   instructor's addendum on that file.

5. General note from Instructor Umino, appended to file at year-end: "Loud, often in
   trouble, chronically behind on the fundamentals he doesn't find interesting. Also
   the most stubborn kid I've ever taught, and it is not a bad kind of stubborn. Keep
   an eye on this one. Recommend against writing him off — have seen worse students
   turn out fine, and this one tries harder than any of them once something actually
   matters to him."

Record closed and archived per Academy policy on Hokage's certification of the
student's genin status.
